usage: phonopy [-h] [--pa PRIMITIVE_AXES [PRIMITIVE_AXES ...]]
               [--tolerance SYMMETRY_TOLERANCE] [--nosym]
               [--magmom MAGMOMS [MAGMOMS ...]]
               [--site-mixture SITE_MIXTURE [SITE_MIXTURE ...]]
               [--split-site-mixture] [--mass MASSES [MASSES ...]]
               [--mass-ase-iupac2016] [--hdf5]
               [--hdf5-compression HDF5_COMPRESSION] [--include-fc]
               [--include-fs] [--include-disp] [--include-all] [--sp]
               [--rd RANDOM_DISPLACEMENTS] [--random-seed RANDOM_SEED] [-q]
               [-v] [--loglevel LOGLEVEL] [--config FILE] [--alm]
               [--anime ANIME [ANIME ...]]
               [--band BAND_PATHS [BAND_PATHS ...]] [--band-connection]
               [--band-const-interval]
               [--band-labels BAND_LABELS [BAND_LABELS ...]]
               [--band-format BAND_FORMAT] [--band-points BAND_POINTS]
               [--bi BAND_INDICES [BAND_INDICES ...]] [--classical]
               [--cutoff-freq CUTOFF_FREQUENCY]
               [--cutoff-radius CUTOFF_RADIUS]
               [--dm-decimals DYNAMICAL_MATRIX_DECIMALS] [--dos] [--eigvecs]
               [--exclude-born] [--factor FREQUENCY_CONVERSION_FACTOR]
               [--fc-calc FC_CALCULATOR] [--fc-calc-opt FC_CALCULATOR_OPTIONS]
               [--fc-decimals FORCE_CONSTANTS_DECIMALS]
               [--fc-format FC_FORMAT] [--fc-spg-symmetry]
               [--fits-debye-model] [--full-fc] [--fmax FMAX] [--fmin FMIN]
               [--fpitch FPITCH] [--gc] [--gv] [--gv-delta-q GV_DELTA_Q]
               [--irreps IRREPS_QPOINT [IRREPS_QPOINT ...]] [--legend]
               [--legacy-plot] [--lcg] [--mesh-format MESH_FORMAT]
               [--modulation MODULATION [MODULATION ...]]
               [--mp MESH_NUMBERS [MESH_NUMBERS ...]]
               [--mlp-params MLP_PARAMS] [--moment]
               [--moment-order MOMENT_ORDER] [--nac-method NAC_METHOD]
               [--no-fc-symmetry] [--nomeshsym] [--nonac] [--noreadfc]
               [--nowritemesh] [-p]
               [--pd PROJECTION_DIRECTION [PROJECTION_DIRECTION ...]]
               [--pdos PDOS [PDOS ...]] [--pr] [--pt] [--pypolymlp]
               [--qpoints QPOINTS [QPOINTS ...]]
               [--qpoints-format QPOINTS_FORMAT]
               [--q-direction NAC_Q_DIRECTION [NAC_Q_DIRECTION ...]]
               [--rd-temperature TEMPERATURE] [--readfc-format READFC_FORMAT]
               [--read-qpoints] [--relax-atomic-positions] [--rust]
               [--legacy-backend] [-s] [--show-irreps] [--sigma SIGMA]
               [--sscha SSCHA_ITERATIONS] [-t] [--td] [--tdm]
               [--tdm-cif TEMPERATURE] [--temperature TEMPERATURE]
               [--tmax TMAX] [--tmin TMIN] [--tstep TSTEP] [--writefc]
               [--writefc-format WRITEFC_FORMAT] [--writedm]
               [--xyz-projection]
               [filename ...]

phonopy: phonon calculation from a phonopy.yaml-like file.

positional arguments:
  filename              phonopy.yaml like file

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --alm                 Use ALM for generating force constants
  --anime ANIME [ANIME ...]
                        Same as ANIME tag
  --band BAND_PATHS [BAND_PATHS ...]
                        Same behavior as BAND tag
  --band-connection     Treat band crossings
  --band-const-interval
                        Band paths are sampled with similar interval.
  --band-format BAND_FORMAT
                        Band structure output file-format
  --band-labels BAND_LABELS [BAND_LABELS ...]
                        Show labels at band segments
  --band-points BAND_POINTS
                        Number of points calculated on a band segment in the
                        band structure mode
  --bi BAND_INDICES [BAND_INDICES ...], --band-indices BAND_INDICES [BAND_INDICES ...]
                        Band indices to be included to calculate thermal
                        properties
  --classical           Compute thermodynamic properties using classical
                        statistics.
  --config FILE         Phonopy configuration file
  --cutoff-freq CUTOFF_FREQUENCY, --cutoff-frequency CUTOFF_FREQUENCY
                        Thermal properties are not calculated below this
                        cutoff frequency.
  --cutoff-radius CUTOFF_RADIUS
                        Out of cutoff radius, force constants are set zero.
  --dm-decimals DYNAMICAL_MATRIX_DECIMALS
                        Decimals of values of decimals
  --dos                 Calculate (P)DOS
  --eigvecs, --eigenvectors
                        Output eigenvectors
  --exclude-born, --exclude-nac-params
                        Exclude born effective charge and dielectric tensor in
                        phonopy.yaml
  --factor FREQUENCY_CONVERSION_FACTOR
                        Frequency unit conversion factor
  --fc-calc FC_CALCULATOR, --fc-calculator FC_CALCULATOR
                        Force constants calculator
  --fc-calc-opt FC_CALCULATOR_OPTIONS, --fc-calculator-options FC_CALCULATOR_OPTIONS
                        Options for force constants calculator as comma
                        separated string with the style of key = values
  --fc-decimals FORCE_CONSTANTS_DECIMALS
                        Decimals of values of force constants
  --fc-format FC_FORMAT
                        Force constants input/output file-format
  --fc-spg-symmetry     Enforce space group symmetry to force constants
  --fits-debye-model    Fits total DOS to a Debye model
  --fmax FMAX           Maximum frequency used for DOS or moment calculation
  --fmin FMIN           Minimum frequency used for DOS or moment calculation
  --fpitch FPITCH       Frequency pitch used for DOS or moment calculation
  --full-fc             Calculate full supercell force constants matrix
  --gc, --gamma-center  Set mesh as Gamma center
  --gv, --group-velocity
                        Calculate group velocities at q-points
  --gv-delta-q GV_DELTA_Q
                        Delta-q distance used for group velocity calculation
  --hdf5                Use hdf5 for force constants
  --hdf5-compression HDF5_COMPRESSION
                        hdf5 compression filter (default: "gzip") and "none"
                        for no compression
  --include-all         Include all output file data in phonopy.yaml
  --include-disp        Include displacements in phonopy.yaml
  --include-fc          Include force constants in phonopy.yaml
  --include-fs          Include force sets in phonopy.yaml
  --irreps IRREPS_QPOINT [IRREPS_QPOINT ...], --irreps-qpoint IRREPS_QPOINT [IRREPS_QPOINT ...]
                        A q-point where characters of irreps are calculated
  --lcg, --little-cogroup
                        Show irreps of little co-group (or point-group of wave
                        vector q) instead of little group
  --legacy-backend      Use the legacy C-extension backend instead of the
                        default Rust backend
  --legacy-plot         Legacy style band structure pl
  --legend              Legend of plots is shown in thermal displacements
  --loglevel LOGLEVEL   Log level
  --magmom MAGMOMS [MAGMOMS ...]
                        Same as MAGMOM tag
  --mass MASSES [MASSES ...]
                        Same as MASS tag
  --mass-ase-iupac2016  Import atomic weights from ASE according to IUPAC 2016
  --mesh-format MESH_FORMAT
                        Mesh output file-format
  --mlp-params MLP_PARAMS
                        Parameters for machine learning potentials as comma
                        separated string with the style of key = values
  --modulation MODULATION [MODULATION ...]
                        Same as MODULATION tag
  --moment              Calculate moment of phonon states distribution
  --moment-order MOMENT_ORDER
                        Order of moment of phonon states distribution
  --mp MESH_NUMBERS [MESH_NUMBERS ...], --mesh MESH_NUMBERS [MESH_NUMBERS ...]
                        Same behavior as MP tag
  --nac-method NAC_METHOD
                        Non-analytical term correction method: Gonze (default)
                        or Wang
  --no-fc-symmetry, --no-sym-fc
                        Do not symmetrize force constants
  --nomeshsym           Symmetry is not imposed for mesh sampling.
  --nonac               Non-analytical term correction
  --noreadfc            Do not read force constants from file
  --nosym               Symmetry is not imposed.
  --nowritemesh         Do not write mesh.yaml or mesh.hdf5
  -p, --plot            Plot data
  --pa PRIMITIVE_AXES [PRIMITIVE_AXES ...], --primitive-axis PRIMITIVE_AXES [PRIMITIVE_AXES ...], --primitive-axes PRIMITIVE_AXES [PRIMITIVE_AXES ...]
                        Same as PRIMITIVE_AXES tag
  --pd PROJECTION_DIRECTION [PROJECTION_DIRECTION ...], --projection-direction PROJECTION_DIRECTION [PROJECTION_DIRECTION ...]
                        Same as PROJECTION_DIRECTION tag
  --pdos PDOS [PDOS ...]
                        Same as PDOS tag
  --pr, --pretend-real  Use imaginary frequency as real for thermal property
                        calculation. For a testing purpose only, when a small
                        amount of imaginary branches obtained.
  --pt, --projected-thermal-property
                        Output projected thermal properties
  --pypolymlp           Use pypolymlp for generating force constants
  -q, --quiet           Print out smallest information
  --q-direction NAC_Q_DIRECTION [NAC_Q_DIRECTION ...]
                        Direction of q-vector perturbation used for NAC at
                        q->0, and group velocity for degenerate phonon mode in
                        q-points mode
  --qpoints QPOINTS [QPOINTS ...]
                        Calculate at specified q-points
  --qpoints-format QPOINTS_FORMAT
                        Q-points output file-format
  --random-seed RANDOM_SEED
                        Random seed by a 32 bit unsigned integer
  --rd RANDOM_DISPLACEMENTS, --random-displacements RANDOM_DISPLACEMENTS
                        Number of supercells with random displacements or
                        "auto".
  --rd-temperature TEMPERATURE
                        A temperature used to generate random displacements.
  --read-qpoints        Read QPOINTS
  --readfc-format READFC_FORMAT
                        Force constants input file-format
  --relax-atomic-positions
                        Relax atomic positions using polynomial MLPs
  --rust                Deprecated no-op: the Rust backend (phonors) is the
                        default in phonopy v4. Pass --legacy-backend to opt
                        back into the C extension.
  -s, --save            Save plot data in pdf
  --show-irreps         Show IR-Reps along with characters
  --sigma SIGMA         Smearing width for DOS
  --site-mixture SITE_MIXTURE [SITE_MIXTURE ...]
                        [Experimental] Per-atom mixture weights in the order
                        atoms appear in the input cell. Weights within each
                        overlapping group of atoms must sum to 1.0. By default
                        the overlapping atoms are merged into mixed-species
                        sites (Virtual Crystal Approximation); pass --split-
                        site-mixture to instead keep them as separate species-
                        resolved atoms. Note that this is per-atom and
                        distinct from the VASP INCAR VCA tag, which lists one
                        weight per element row in POSCAR.
  --sp, --save-params   Save parameters that can run phonopy in
                        phonopy_params.yaml.
  --split-site-mixture  [Experimental] With --site-mixture, keep overlapping
                        atoms as separate species-resolved atoms instead of
                        merging them into mixed-species sites.
  --sscha SSCHA_ITERATIONS
                        Number of iterations in SSCHA calculation
  -t, --thermal-property
                        Output thermal properties
  --td, --thermal-displacements
                        Output thermal displacements
  --tdm, --thermal-displacement-matrix
                        Output thermal displacement matrices
  --tdm-cif TEMPERATURE, --thermal-displacement-matrix-cif TEMPERATURE
                        Write cif with aniso_U for which temperature is
                        specified
  --temperature TEMPERATURE
                        (Deprecated) A temperature used to generate random
                        displacements.
  --tmax TMAX           Maximum calculated temperature
  --tmin TMIN           Minimum calculated temperature
  --tolerance SYMMETRY_TOLERANCE
                        Symmetry tolerance to search
  --tstep TSTEP         Calculated temperature step
  -v, --verbose         Detailed information is shown.
  --writedm             Write dynamical matrices. This has to be used with
                        QPOINTS setting (or --qpoints)
  --writefc             Write FORCE_CONSTANTS
  --writefc-format WRITEFC_FORMAT
                        Force constants output file-format
  --xyz-projection      Project PDOS x, y, z directions in Cartesian
                        coordinates
